## Planning implications

| Work item | Status |
|---|---|
| Infrastructure: `DeviceSettingsClient` + Pigeon + AKW/BK adapters | **Done** |
| Delete raw settings builders/senders | **Done** (`9634a25f`) |
| `feature_device_album` multimedia settings | **Migrated** |
| `feature_device_settings.setVolume` | **Migrated** (controller only; no volume UI on settings page yet) |
| Settings page UI: wear detection, voice wakeup, guide, auto power-off, key definition | **Placeholder `showSoon`** — wire to typed client |
| `sendKeyDefine` (`0x34/0x02`) | Still raw; **not** in `DeviceSettingsClient` — separate capability if needed |
| Wi-Fi scan toggle (`setWifiScan`) | Still raw in `common_ble_protocol`; family Wi-Fi uses `DeviceNetworkSettingsClient` instead |
| Stale docs | Update `feature_device_settings/README.md`, `specs/capabilities/app_llm.md` L51 (still references deleted `switchWakeup`) |

For a new settings instruction migration, the precedent is: add/confirm SDK typed API in runtime → migrate Feature call sites → delete raw builder/sender in same PR → record bytes in Git/0035. **Settings slice 1 already followed this path.**
